    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `capacityWarning` flag that is `true` when an owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), following the codebase's existing pattern for create-time-computed, read-visible fields (`possibleDuplicate`, `householdGold`).\n\nChanges, all as small cohesive units:\n\n1. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** \u2014 added one new static method `isApproachingCapacity(...)` alongside the existing capacity logic, reusing the same `normalize(...)` helper and the `CITY_CAPACITY` constant, plus a new `CITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40`. The hard rejection at 50 is untouched.\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added line that computes the warning on the pre-save owner list (mirroring how `bulkSignupWarning` is computed before save) and sets it on the entity.\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 a `capacity_warning` field with trivial getter/setter (mirrors `householdGold`), so MapStruct auto-maps it to the DTO on both create and `GET`.\n4. **`schema.sql`** \u2014 the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column (only the hsqldb schema carries these sibling columns).\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 the read-only `capacityWarning` property so the generated DTO exposes it.\n\nKey correctness detail I caught during testing: the warning must be evaluated on the **pre-save** owner list and **persisted**, because the acceptance test reads the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (a live-computed-after-save value counted the new owner itself and wasn't visible on read).",
